            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "# How to use this workbook\n\n**Purpose:** technical readiness review of **SQL Server enabled by Azure Arc** (Azure extension for SQL Server on Arc-enabled servers) for a move to **pay-as-you-go (PAYG)**. It only reads Azure Resource Graph and changes nothing. Scope is Azure Arc only; Azure VMs are outside `-Target Arc`.\n\n> Informational only. It does not prove Software Assurance entitlement, billing, CSP consent or compliance. Confirm charges in Cost Management and entitlement through the customer licensing process. Core numbers are estimates, not meters.\n\n## Quick path (direct links)\nUse the buttons below the text to jump to each tab.\n1. **Summary** (button *1*): footprint, license mix, tiles.\n2. **PAYG review** (button *2*): start with 🔴 hosts; see what the script would convert.\n3. **Validation** (button *3*): ESU, CSP consent, connectivity, pCore.\n4. Run the script with `-ReportOnly` and reconcile: [manage-payg-transition.ps1](https://github.com/microsoft/sql-server-samples/blob/e1163bff690ef8b3109d83dd139ffdf1a40219da/samples/manage/manage-payg-transition/manage-payg-transition.ps1) · [README](https://github.com/microsoft/sql-server-samples/blob/master/samples/manage/manage-payg-transition/README.md) · [Learn: PAYG transition](https://learn.microsoft.com/sql/sql-server/azure-arc/manage-pay-as-you-go-transition).\n5. Pilot a small approved set with `-WaitForCompletion` (same script).\n6. Confirm in [Cost Management](https://portal.azure.com/#view/Microsoft_Azure_CostManagement/Menu/~/costanalysis) and set the auto-deploy tag: [Learn: auto-deploy](https://learn.microsoft.com/sql/sql-server/azure-arc/manage-autodeploy).\n\n## Tabs\n| Tab | Use it for |\n|---|---|\n| **Summary** | Tiles, license mix, versions and support status |\n| **PAYG review** | Per-host priority, what the script would convert, next action; reconciliation backlog |\n| **Inventory** | Full exportable evidence |\n| **Architecture / cores** | VM vs physical signal, core estimate, pCore and unlimited virtualization options |\n| **Validations** | Auto-deploy tags, missing extension, ESU, CSP consent, connectivity, SQLServerLicense and pCore alignment |\n| **References** | Official links and execution flow |\n\n## Priority\n🔴 **High**: Arc not connected, extension missing or not Succeeded, or the script would convert LicenseOnly, Server+CAL or pCore hosts. 🟠 **Medium**: HADR, free/test, license type not set, SQL discovery not true, SQL 2014/2016 without ESU, other-cloud VM. 🟢 **OK**: no blocker found by metadata.\n\n## Core estimate (not billing)\nUsage is metered per operating system environment, minimum 4 cores; the Standard compute-capacity approximation is 24 through 2022 and 32 for 2025, not a billing cap; Developer, Evaluation and Express are not billed; passive HA/DR candidates count 0 on Windows, but on Linux all instances are billed as active. VM uses vCPU, bare metal uses physical cores. Hosts with pCore applied may be covered by a physical core license.\n\n## What the script really does (source commit e1163bf and Microsoft Learn)\n- Selects every machine with SQL discovered, a Microsoft.AzureData extension in Succeeded and `LicenseType != PAYG`. That includes **Paid, LicenseOnly, Server+CAL and unset** hosts.\n- `-UsePcoreLicense` defaults to **No**: hosts with pCore applied are unset.\n- The wrapper does **not** pass recurring consent or exclusion tags. For CSP subscriptions use the Azure Policy \"Arc-enabled SQL Server license type compliance\" or `modify-license-type.ps1 -LicenseType PAYG -ConsentToRecurringPAYG Yes`.\n- Without `-targetSubscription` the scope is every accessible subscription in the tenant. Pass `-TenantId`.\n- Without `-WaitForCompletion` a result of `RequestSubmitted` means accepted, not applied.\n- README: Disconnected or Expired agents cannot be updated. The README also mentions tagging subscriptions with `ArcSQLServerExtensionDeployment:PAYG`; the code in the analyzed commit does not apply it, so set the tag yourself.\n\n## Glossary\n**PAYG** hourly pay-as-you-go. **Paid** attests SA or SQL subscription. **LicenseOnly** perpetual, free, SPLA or Server+CAL. **pCore** physical core license with unlimited virtualization (Enterprise). **OSE** operating system environment. **ESU** Extended Security Updates. **ReportOnly** script dry run.\n"
            },
