    {
      "type": 12,
      "content": {
        "version": "NotebookGroup/1.0",
        "groupType": "editable",
        "items": [
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "## Architecture / cores (signals, not prices)\nLive Azure Resource Graph metadata only; rows are per Arc guest or bare-metal machine, not per hypervisor host.\n- **VM:** review vCPU allocation separately from engine capacity and actual billing.\n- **Bare metal:** billed on physical cores; confirm sockets and cores per socket (hyperthreads are not cores).\n- **Unlimited virtualization:** Enterprise `SQLServerLicense` covering physical cores of every eligible host (min 16 cores), all VMs connected to Arc in scope with `UsePhysicalCoreLicense` = true and LicenseType = billingPlan. Not available for VMs on listed other providers. Physical machines without VMs in scope get no benefit. Never infer host cores from vCPUs; formula: sum of sockets x physical cores per socket per eligible host.\n- Compare prices only with current official pricing and Cost Management. This workbook does not quote.\n\n\n**Core-estimate method (verified on 2026-11-06):** the Standard compute-capacity approximation is 24 cores through SQL Server 2022 and 32 for SQL Server 2025, based only on Standard instances on that machine. Unknown editions or missing core counts remain unknown, not zero. This is not a license requirement or an Azure billing meter: compute capacity, OSE allocation and billed cores are different concepts; reconcile physical-host and VM licensing with [Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/sql/sql-server/azure-arc/manage-license-billing) and [edition capacity limits](https://learn.microsoft.com/sql/sql-server/compute-capacity-limits-by-edition-of-sql-server)."
            },
            "name": "architecture_guide",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "Language",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "EN"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "## Arquitetura / núcleos (sinais, não preços)\nSomente metadados atuais do Azure Resource Graph; cada linha é uma máquina Arc convidada ou bare metal, não um host de hipervisor.\n- **VM:** revise a alocação de vCPUs separadamente da capacidade do mecanismo e da cobrança real.\n- **Bare metal:** cobrado por núcleos físicos; confirme sockets e núcleos por socket (hyperthreads não são núcleos).\n- **Virtualização ilimitada:** `SQLServerLicense` Enterprise cobrindo os núcleos físicos de todos os hosts elegíveis (mín. 16 núcleos), com todas as VMs conectadas ao Arc no escopo, `UsePhysicalCoreLicense` = true e LicenseType = billingPlan. Indisponível para VMs em outros provedores listados. Máquina física sem VMs no escopo não recebe o benefício. Nunca deduza núcleos do host a partir de vCPUs; fórmula: soma de sockets x núcleos físicos por socket de cada host elegível.\n- Compare preços somente com a tabela oficial atual e o Cost Management. Este workbook não cotiza.\n\n\n**Método da estimativa de núcleos (verificado em 2026-11-06):** a aproximação da capacidade Standard é de 24 núcleos até SQL Server 2022 e 32 para SQL Server 2025, considerando apenas as instâncias Standard da máquina. Edição ou quantidade de núcleos desconhecida continua desconhecida, não zero. Não representa requisito de licença nem medidor de cobrança Azure: capacidade do mecanismo, alocação da OSE e núcleos faturados são conceitos distintos; reconcilie licenciamento de hosts físicos e VMs com o [Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/sql/sql-server/azure-arc/manage-license-billing) e os [limites por edição](https://learn.microsoft.com/sql/sql-server/compute-capacity-limits-by-edition-of-sql-server)."
            },
            "name": "architecture_guide-pt",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "Language",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "PT"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "resources\n| where type =~ 'microsoft.azurearcdata/sqlserverinstances'\n| extend HostId = tolower(tostring(properties.containerResourceId))\n| where HostId contains '/providers/microsoft.hybridcompute/machines/'\n| extend Edition=tostring(properties.edition), Version=tostring(properties.version), InstanceLicenseType=tostring(properties.licenseType)\n| extend EditionRank = case(Edition has 'Enterprise', 6, Edition has 'Standard', 5, Edition has 'Web', 4, Edition has 'Express', 3, Edition has 'Developer', 2, Edition has 'Evaluation', 1, 0)\n| extend SqlVersionMajor = case(Version has 'SQL Server 2014' or Version startswith '12.', 'SQL Server 2014', Version has 'SQL Server 2016' or Version startswith '13.', 'SQL Server 2016', Version has 'SQL Server 2017' or Version startswith '14.', 'SQL Server 2017', Version has 'SQL Server 2019' or Version startswith '15.', 'SQL Server 2019', Version has 'SQL Server 2022' or Version startswith '16.', 'SQL Server 2022', Version has 'SQL Server 2025' or Version startswith '17.', 'SQL Server 2025', isnotempty(Version), Version, 'Not identified')\n| summarize Instances=count(), ActiveInstances=countif(InstanceLicenseType !~ 'HADR'), HadrInstances=countif(InstanceLicenseType =~ 'HADR'), FreeOrTestInstances=countif(Edition has 'Developer' or Edition has 'Evaluation' or Edition has 'Express'), ServerCALInstances=countif(InstanceLicenseType =~ 'ServerCAL'), EsuVersionInstances=countif(SqlVersionMajor in ('SQL Server 2014','SQL Server 2016')), TopEditionRank=max(EditionRank), StandardCoreLimit=max(iff(Edition has 'Standard', iff(SqlVersionMajor == 'SQL Server 2025', 32, 24), 0)), Editions=make_set(Edition), Versions=make_set(SqlVersionMajor), InstanceLicenseTypes=make_set(InstanceLicenseType) by HostId\n| extend TopEdition = case(TopEditionRank == 6, 'Enterprise', TopEditionRank == 5, 'Standard', TopEditionRank == 4, 'Web', TopEditionRank == 3, 'Express', TopEditionRank == 2, 'Developer', TopEditionRank == 1, 'Evaluation', 'Not identified')\n| extend HadrOnlySignal = Instances > 0 and ActiveInstances == 0\n| join kind=leftouter (\n    resources\n    | where type =~ 'microsoft.hybridcompute/machines'\n    | extend HostId = tolower(id)\n    | project HostId, MachineName=tostring(name), ArcStatus=tostring(properties.status), SqlDiscovered=tostring(properties.detectedProperties.mssqldiscovered), LogicalCoreCount=toint(properties.detectedProperties.logicalCoreCount), PhysicalCoreCount=toint(properties.detectedProperties.coreCount), SocketCount=toint(properties.detectedProperties.processorCount), Manufacturer=tostring(properties.detectedProperties.manufacturer), HardwareModel=tostring(properties.detectedProperties.model), OsType=tostring(properties.osType), OsName=tostring(properties.osName), LastStatusChange=todatetime(properties.lastStatusChange), MachineRG=resourceGroup, MachineSub=subscriptionId\n) on HostId\n| join kind=leftouter (\n    resources\n    | where type =~ 'microsoft.hybridcompute/machines/extensions'\n    | where tostring(properties.publisher) =~ 'Microsoft.AzureData'\n    | where tostring(properties.type) in~ ('WindowsAgent.SqlServer','LinuxAgent.SqlServer')\n    | extend HostId = tolower(substring(id, 0, indexof(tolower(id), '/extensions')))\n    | extend HostLicenseTypeRaw = tostring(properties.settings.LicenseType)\n    | extend HostLicenseType = case(HostLicenseTypeRaw =~ 'PAYG', 'PAYG', HostLicenseTypeRaw =~ 'Paid', 'Paid', HostLicenseTypeRaw =~ 'LicenseOnly', 'LicenseOnly', isempty(HostLicenseTypeRaw), 'Not reported', HostLicenseTypeRaw)\n    | extend UsePhysicalCoreLicenseRaw = tostring(properties.settings.UsePhysicalCoreLicense.IsApplied)\n    | extend UsePhysicalCoreLicense = case(UsePhysicalCoreLicenseRaw =~ 'true', 'Applied', UsePhysicalCoreLicenseRaw =~ 'false', 'Not applied', 'Not reported')\n    | project HostId, ExtensionState=tostring(properties.provisioningState), ExtensionVersion=tostring(properties.typeHandlerVersion), HostLicenseType, EnableESU=tostring(properties.settings.enableExtendedSecurityUpdates), UsePhysicalCoreLicense, RecurringPAYGConsent=tostring(properties.settings.ConsentToRecurringPAYG.Consented), RecurringPAYGConsentTimestamp=tostring(properties.settings.ConsentToRecurringPAYG.ConsentTimestamp)\n) on HostId\n| join kind=leftouter (\n    resources\n    | where type =~ 'microsoft.hybridcompute/machines/extensions'\n    | where tostring(properties.publisher) =~ 'Microsoft.AzureData'\n    | where tostring(properties.provisioningState) == 'Succeeded'\n    | where tostring(properties.settings.LicenseType) != 'PAYG'\n    | extend HostId=tolower(substring(id,0,indexof(id,'/extensions')))\n    | summarize ScriptExtensionMatches=count(), ScriptMatchedExtensionTypes=make_set(tostring(properties.type)) by HostId\n) on HostId\n| extend HostLicenseType=coalesce(HostLicenseType,'Not reported'), UsePhysicalCoreLicense=coalesce(UsePhysicalCoreLicense,'Not reported'), ScriptExtensionMatches=coalesce(ScriptExtensionMatches,0)\n| extend ResourceGroup=coalesce(MachineRG, tostring(split(HostId,'/')[4])), SubscriptionId=coalesce(MachineSub, tostring(split(HostId,'/')[2]))\n| extend IsLinux = OsType =~ 'linux'\n| extend HwText = tolower(strcat(HardwareModel, ' ', Manufacturer))\n| extend IsVm = HwText contains 'virtual' or HwText contains 'vmware' or HwText contains 'kvm' or HwText contains 'hvm' or HwText contains 'standard pc' or HwText contains 'google' or HwText contains 'nutanix' or HwText contains 'openstack' or HwText contains 'amazon' or HwText contains 'bhyve' or HwText contains 'xen' or HwText contains 'qemu' or HwText contains 'innotek' or HwText contains 'red hat'\n| extend ForeignCloud = HwText contains 'amazon' or HwText contains 'google'\n| extend FormFactor = case(IsVm, 'VM', isnotempty(HardwareModel) and isnotempty(Manufacturer), 'PHYSICAL', 'UNKNOWN')\n| extend RawCores = iff(FormFactor == 'PHYSICAL', coalesce(PhysicalCoreCount, LogicalCoreCount), coalesce(LogicalCoreCount, PhysicalCoreCount))\n| extend CoreEstimate = case(\n    TopEdition in ('Express','Developer','Evaluation') or (HadrOnlySignal and not(IsLinux)), tolong(0),\n    TopEdition == 'Not identified' or isnull(RawCores) or RawCores <= 0, long(null),\n    TopEdition == 'Standard', tolong(max_of(4, min_of(RawCores, StandardCoreLimit))),\n    tolong(max_of(4, RawCores)))\n| extend ReviewCode = case(\n    HostLicenseType == 'Paid' and TopEdition in ('Enterprise','Standard') and ActiveInstances > 0, 'PAID_REVIEW',\n    HostLicenseType == 'Paid' and HadrOnlySignal, 'PAID_HADR',\n    HostLicenseType == 'PAYG', 'ALREADY_PAYG',\n    HostLicenseType == 'LicenseOnly', 'LICENSEONLY',\n    HostLicenseType == 'Not reported', 'NOT_REPORTED',\n    FreeOrTestInstances > 0, 'FREE_TEST',\n    'REVIEW')\n| extend ScriptCode = case(isempty(MachineName), 'NO_MACHINE', SqlDiscovered !~ 'true', 'NO_DISCOVERY', ScriptExtensionMatches > 0, 'MATCH', 'NO_EXT')\n| extend RiskIfConverted = ScriptCode == 'MATCH' and (HostLicenseType =~ 'LicenseOnly' or ServerCALInstances > 0 or UsePhysicalCoreLicense == 'Applied')\n| extend PriorityNum = case(\n    isempty(MachineName) or ArcStatus !~ 'Connected' or isempty(ExtensionState) or ExtensionState !~ 'Succeeded' or RiskIfConverted, 1,\n    HadrInstances > 0 or FreeOrTestInstances > 0 or HostLicenseType == 'Not reported' or SqlDiscovered !~ 'true' or (EsuVersionInstances > 0 and EnableESU !~ 'true') or ForeignCloud or ServerCALInstances > 0, 2,\n    3)\n| extend Priority = case(PriorityNum == 1, iff('{Language}'=='PT', '🔴 Alta', '🔴 High'), PriorityNum == 2, iff('{Language}'=='PT', '🟠 Média', '🟠 Medium'), iff('{Language}'=='PT', '🟢 OK', '🟢 OK'))\n| order by PriorityNum asc, MachineName asc\n| extend ModelOption = case(\n    FormFactor == 'VM' and ForeignCloud, iff('{Language}'=='PT', 'VM em outro provedor: licenciar só por vCore; virtualização ilimitada indisponível', 'VM on another cloud: license by vCore only; unlimited virtualization unavailable'),\n    FormFactor == 'VM' and UsePhysicalCoreLicense == 'Applied', iff('{Language}'=='PT', 'VM com pCore: valide SQLServerLicense Enterprise (ativa, escopo, billingPlan = LicenseType) e todos os hosts elegíveis', 'VM with pCore: verify Enterprise SQLServerLicense (active, scope, billingPlan = LicenseType) and all eligible hosts'),\n    FormFactor == 'VM', iff('{Language}'=='PT', 'VM: valide vCPUs e cobrança real; a capacidade Standard depende da versão, não é teto de cobrança. Virtualização ilimitada exige inventário completo dos hosts', 'VM: reconcile vCPUs and actual billing; Standard capacity is version-dependent, not a billing cap. Unlimited virtualization requires full host inventory'),\n    FormFactor == 'PHYSICAL' and UsePhysicalCoreLicense == 'Applied', iff('{Language}'=='PT', 'Servidor físico com pCore: sem benefício de virtualização ilimitada sem VMs no escopo', 'Physical server with pCore: no unlimited-virtualization benefit without VMs in scope'),\n    FormFactor == 'PHYSICAL', iff('{Language}'=='PT', 'Físico: confirme sockets, núcleos físicos e cobrança real; a capacidade Standard depende da versão, não é teto de cobrança', 'Physical: confirm sockets, physical cores and actual billing; Standard capacity is version-dependent, not a billing cap'),\n    iff('{Language}'=='PT', 'Desconhecido: colete evidência de hipervisor ou hardware', 'Unknown: collect hypervisor or hardware evidence'))\n| project id=HostId, Priority, MachineName=iff(isempty(MachineName), HostId, MachineName), ResourceGroup, SubscriptionId, FormFactor, Manufacturer, HardwareModel, OsType, SocketCount, PhysicalCoreCount, LogicalCoreCount, CoreEstimateNotBilling=CoreEstimate, TopEdition, HostLicenseType, UsePhysicalCoreLicense, ArcStatus, ExtensionState, ModelOption\n",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Architecture and core signals / Sinais de arquitetura e núcleos",
              "noDataMessage": "No rows returned for the selected subscriptions. / Nenhuma linha para as assinaturas selecionadas.",
              "showExportToExcel": true,
              "queryType": 1,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.resourcegraph/resources",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Subscription}"
              ],
              "visualization": "table",
              "gridSettings": {
                "rowLimit": 10000,
                "filter": true
              }
            },
            "name": "architecture_options"
          }
        ]
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "SelectedTab",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "Architecture"
      },
      "name": "tab-group-Architecture"
    },
    {
      "type": 12,
      "content": {
        "version": "NotebookGroup/1.0",
        "groupType": "editable",
        "items": [
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "## SQL Server on Azure VMs (Microsoft.SqlVirtualMachine)\nThese queries read the SQL IaaS extension resources of **Azure VMs**, not Arc-enabled servers. The license type has three documented values: PAYG, AHUB (Azure Hybrid Benefit, requires Software Assurance) and DR (free HA/DR replica) ([Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-sql/virtual-machines/windows/licensing-model-azure-hybrid-benefit-ahb-change), checked on 2026-11-10; property names and values checked against the `Microsoft.SqlVirtualMachine` 2023-10-01 API spec). Developer and Express editions are free and listed separately. The workbook cannot see Software Assurance, so PAYG rows are review candidates, not recommendations. vCore counts are not available in Azure Resource Graph and are not shown.\n"
            },
            "name": "azvm_note",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "Language",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "EN"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "## SQL Server em VMs do Azure (Microsoft.SqlVirtualMachine)\nEstas consultas leem os recursos da extensão SQL IaaS de **VMs do Azure**, não de servidores habilitados pelo Arc. O tipo de licença tem três valores documentados: PAYG, AHUB (Azure Hybrid Benefit, exige Software Assurance) e DR (réplica HA/DR gratuita) ([Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/azure-sql/virtual-machines/windows/licensing-model-azure-hybrid-benefit-ahb-change), verificado em 10/11/2026; nomes e valores das propriedades conferidos no spec de API `Microsoft.SqlVirtualMachine` 2023-10-01). As edições Developer e Express são gratuitas e aparecem separadas. O workbook não enxerga Software Assurance, então linhas PAYG são candidatas à revisão, não recomendações. A quantidade de vCores não está no Azure Resource Graph e não é exibida.\n"
            },
            "name": "azvm_note-pt",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "Language",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "PT"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "resources\n| where type =~ 'microsoft.sqlvirtualmachine/sqlvirtualmachines'\n| extend Edition=iff(isempty(tostring(properties.sqlImageSku)), 'Not reported', tostring(properties.sqlImageSku)), LicenseType=iff(isempty(tostring(properties.sqlServerLicenseType)), 'Not reported', tostring(properties.sqlServerLicenseType))\n| extend Scope=iff(Edition in~ ('Developer','Express'), iff('{Language}'=='PT', 'Edição gratuita', 'Free edition'), iff('{Language}'=='PT', 'Edição paga ou não informada', 'Paid or unreported edition'))\n| summarize SqlVMs=count() by Scope, Edition, LicenseType\n| order by Scope asc, Edition asc, LicenseType asc\n",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "SQL Server on Azure VMs by license type / SQL Server em VMs Azure por tipo de licença",
              "noDataMessage": "No rows returned for the selected subscriptions. / Nenhuma linha para as assinaturas selecionadas.",
              "showExportToExcel": true,
              "queryType": 1,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.resourcegraph/resources",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Subscription}"
              ],
              "visualization": "table",
              "gridSettings": {
                "rowLimit": 1000,
                "filter": true
              }
            },
            "name": "azvm_summary"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
